  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IJR, Core Support, 2022 - 2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IJR, Core Support, 2022 - 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The IJR works with the broad goal to build of societies that are fair, inclusive, democratic, and peaceful - in contexts that are currently afflicted by conflict or where societies continue to grapple with the historical legacy of such conflicts.  Towards meeting this objective, IJR works with three key outcome areas:

-  Policy actors use peace building and governance research in policy processes.
-  Communities demonstrating agency in transforming relations in divided communities
-  Stakeholders implement transitional justice policies, programs, and processes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Institute for Justice and Reconciliation (IJR) har beg&#xe4;rt k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;rande av sitt program under strategiperioden 2021-2025. IJR &#xe4;r sedan tidigare en partnerorganisation till Sida, vilket inkluderar de senaste tv&#xe5; strategiperioderna, och arbetar f&#xf6;r r&#xe4;ttvisa, inkluderande, demokratiska och fredliga samh&#xe4;llen i Afrika genom arbeta fram relevanta interventioner som kombinerar forskning, dialog, kapacitetsbyggande, opinionsbildning, policyr&#xe5;dgivning samt st&#xf6;d till genomf&#xf6;rande.

IJR arbetar utifr&#xe5;n ett brett m&#xe5;l om att bygga r&#xe4;ttvisa, inkluderande, demokratiska och fredliga samh&#xe4;llen i kontexter p&#xe5;verkade av r&#xe5;dande konflikter eller d&#xe4;r samh&#xe4;llen forts&#xe4;tter att k&#xe4;mpa med det historiska arvet fr&#xe5;n tidigare s&#xe5;dana konflikter. IJR arbetar med fem nyckelomr&#xe5;den, vilka inkluderar:

- Deltagare har f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att anv&#xe4;nda mekanismer f&#xf6;r &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsr&#xe4;ttvisa som &#xe4;r kontextuellt l&#xe4;mpliga

- Deltagare &#xe4;r motiverade att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra r&#xe4;ttvisa, inkludering och fred

- Deltagare vidtar &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som leder till uppr&#xe4;tth&#xe5;llen fred, r&#xe4;ttvisa och f&#xf6;rsoning

- Samh&#xe4;llen &#xe4;r mer motst&#xe5;ndskraftiga, f&#xf6;rsonade och socialt sammanh&#xe5;llda.

- System och policyer bidrar till realiseringen av r&#xe4;ttvisa, inkluderande, demokratiska och fredliga samh&#xe4;llen. 

IJR kommer att arbeta med fem tematiska omr&#xe5;den vilka fokuserar p&#xe5; social sammanh&#xe5;llning, inkludering och antirasism; fr&#xe4;mja m&#xe4;nsklig v&#xe4;rdighet och f&#xf6;rsoning p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5;, &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ngsr&#xe4;ttvisa centrerad kring &#xf6;verlevare; socioekonomisk r&#xe4;ttvisa och inkluderande utveckling samt gr&#xe4;ns&#xf6;verskridande dialog och regional f&#xf6;rsoning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Institute for Justice and Reconciliation (IJR) has requested for core support towards implementing its programmes under the strategy period form 2021 - 2025. IJR has been partnering with Sida in the past including the last two strategy periods and it is working towards fair, inclusive, democratic, and peaceful societies in Africa by designing relevant interventions combining research, dialogue, capacity building, advocacy, policy advice and implementation support.

The IJR works with the broad goal to build of societies that are fair, inclusive, democratic and peaceful - in contexts that are currently afflicted by conflict or where societies continue to grapple with the historical legacy of such conflicts. IJR works with five key outcome areas including:

-  Participants have the capacity to use contextually appropriate transitional justice mechanisms

-  Participants are motivated to enable fairness, inclusivity and peace

-  Participants take actions that lead to sustained peace, justice and reconciliation

-  Communities are more resilient, reconciled and socially cohesive

-  Systems and policies enable the realisation of fair, inclusive, democratic and peaceful societies

IJR will work on five thematic areas that focuses on social cohesion, inclusion and anti-racism; advancing human dignity and bottom-up reconciliation; survivor-centred transitional justice and reconciliation; socio-economic justice and inclusive development; and cross-border dialogue and regional reconciliation.</narrative>
  </description>
